+### `applyPatch(document, patch)`
+
+Implements JSON Patch (RFC 6902) with the operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`
+(section 4). Returns the patched document as a new value; neither `document` nor `patch` is modified, and the
+patch is atomic (section 5): if any operation fails, the error is thrown and nothing is returned. Throws
+`JsonPatchError` if the patch is not an array of valid operations (missing/ill-typed `op`, `path`, `from` or
+`value`, unknown `op`) or an operation fails (missing target, array index out of range or not canonical,
+failed `test`, `move` from a proper prefix of its path, removing the document root). A malformed or
+unresolvable pointer throws `JsonPointerError`. `-` is only valid as the final token of an `add` path.
+Members named `__proto__`, `constructor` etc. are ordinary keys and never touch prototypes.
